hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"137","[AI-translation] Abdullah bin Abdur Rahman bin Abi Sa'sa'ah (Rahimahullah) se riwayat hai, unhon ne kaha: Main ne apne walid se suna, jabke woh Abu Sa'id Khudri [Raziyallahu anhu] ki god mein soe hue the, unhon ne kaha: Mujh se Abu Sa'id ne kaha: Ai mere bete, jab tum in junglon mein ho to azan buland aawaz se kaho; kyunke main ne Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ko farmate suna: 'Use koi insan, jinn, patthar aur darakht nahin sunta magar woh us ke liye gawahi deta hai.'"
"138","[AI-translation] Abdur Rahman bin Abi Sa'sa'ah ke walid (Rahimahullah) se riwayat hai ke unhon ne use khabar di ke Abu Sa'id Khudri [Raziyallahu anhu] ne un se kaha: 'Beshak main tumhen bakriyan aur jungle pasand karte dekhta hun; jab tum apni bakriyon mein ya apne jungle mein ho aur namaz ke liye azan kaho to pukar buland aawaz se kaho; kyunke muazzin ki aawaz ki door tak koi jinn, insan aur cheez nahin sunti magar woh qayamat ke din us ke liye gawahi deti hai.' Abu Sa'id ne kaha: Main ne use Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) se suna."
"139","[AI-translation] Hazrat Maimunah (Raziyallahu anha) se riwayat hai, unhon ne kaha: Nabi (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ek chadar [mirt] mein namaz padhte jis ka ba'z hissa mujh par aur ba'z Aap par hota, jabke main haiza hoti."
"140","[AI-translation] Hazrat Aishah (Raziyallahu anha) se riwayat hai, unhon ne kaha: Main Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ke sar mein kanghi karti jabke main haiza hoti."
"141","[AI-translation] Hazrat Aishah (Raziyallahu anha) se riwayat hai, unhon ne kaha: Main Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ke sar mein kanghi karti jabke main haiza hoti."
"142","[AI-translation] Hazrat Aishah (Raziyallahu anha) se riwayat hai, unhon ne kaha: Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) masjid mein e'tikaf farma hote, phir Apna sar meri taraf nikalte; to main use dhoti jabke main haiza hoti."
"143","[AI-translation] Hazrat Anas bin Malik (Raziyallahu anhu) se riwayat hai, unhon ne kaha: Main ne Rasulullah (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ko farmate suna: 'Jab raat ka khana hazir ho aur namaz ki iqamat kahi jae to pehle khana khao.'"
"144","[AI-translation] Hazrat Aishah (Raziyallahu anha) se riwayat hai ke Nabi (Sallallahu alaihi wasallam) ne farmaya: 'Jab raat ka khana rakha jae aur namaz ki iqamat kahi jae to pehle khana khao.' Aur Shafi'i (Rahimahullah) ne farmaya: Logon ko jama'at mein namaz mein hazir hone ka hukm diya gaya jama'at ki akele par fazeelat ki wajah se; aur jama'at se peeche rehne mein ek ma'na ki wajah se rukhsat di gayi: Woh yeh ke un mein se kisi ka raat ka khana hazir ho aur namaz ki iqamat kahi jae, ya namaz ki iqamat kahi jae jabke use maujooda hajat ke sath wuzu ki zaroorat ho. Aur use mana kiya gaya hai ke woh namaz padhe jabke woh do gandagiyon: Pakhane aur peshab ko rok raha ho. Agar woh namaz padh le to us ki namaz us ki taraf se kafi hai; lekin use uzr ki wajah se jama'at chhorne mein rukhsat hai. Aur us ke liye pasandida hai ke woh namaz mein dakhil ho jabke us ke dil ko us se koi mashgala na ho aur use mukammal karne se koi jaldi na ho. Aksar jo log jante hain woh yeh hai ke jab woh us mein dakhil hota hai jabke use hajat poori karne mein jaldi ki zaroorat hai, to qareeb hai ke woh do baten jama kare: Mukammal karne se jaldi aur tawajjuh se mashguli. Aur is ka khauf us par hai jis ka raat ka khana hazir ho, logon ki khane ki hajat aur un ke nafs ke us ki taraf maail hone ki wajah se, khaas taur par roze dar aur khane ki hajat wale."
